From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa: combined VLAN STRIP+INSERT (translate) HMTD for routed-VLAN

T-M6-8 VLAN throughput investigation (board evidence, 2026-08-31).

fman_hm_vlan_route_get() took a single `bool is_push` and could only ever
build a PUSH-only or POP-only combined HMTD, never both. Every caller
(ask_vlan_cc_flow_add()) only inspected ASK_VLANF_PUSH, so a flow with BOTH
ASK_VLANF_POP and ASK_VLANF_PUSH set -- a same-port VID-to-VID TRANSLATE,
e.g. two 802.1Q vifs (VLAN 6 <-> VLAN 8) on one physical port routing to
each other -- silently got a PUSH-only HMTD that never stripped the
ingress tag.

Board reproduction (8-stream bidirectional iperf3 across two VLANs on one
physical port): ~1M TCP retransmissions for ~6 GB transferred, eth3
rx_dropped climbing by thousands during the run, and 30 distinct
flow-offload cookies observed for a test that should only ever produce
~16 -- consistent with malformed frames on the wire driving TCP resets,
which floods conntrack/nf_flowtable churn and exhausts the per-port
CC-tree's FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS(32) cap (see the companion OOT fix in
ask_vlan_cc.c, commit 21b774da).

Replace `bool is_push` with independent `bool do_pop, bool do_push`
throughout fman_hm_vlan_route_get()/_lookup()/_ent: POP-only and PUSH-only
behave exactly as before; BOTH set builds a 5-op translate chain
{VLAN_STRIP, RMV_ETHERNET, INSRT_GENERIC(L2), IPV4_FORWARD, VLAN_INSERT}
-- strip the old tag, rebuild L2/L3 (unchanged from the existing single-edit
path), insert the new tag last so it rides the rebuilt header, matching the
vendor fill_actions op-order convention already documented for the
single-edit cases. Neither flag set is now explicitly rejected with
-EINVAL (previously silently built a same-thing-as-POP-only spec). Still
within FMAN_HM_MAX_OPS(8).

The refcounted dedup cache key gains do_pop as a discriminant alongside the
existing do_push (renamed from is_push); PUSH-only fields (vid/tpid/pcp)
still only participate in the match when do_push is set, matching the prior
behaviour for that case.

Companion change (separate commit, OOT ask.ko): ask_vlan_cc_flow_add()
threads key->vlan_edit_flags' POP and PUSH bits independently instead of
collapsing them into one is_push bool.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (changed exported API; T-M6-8 VLAN R4d)
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c
index 2bf50c641..3ad140772 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c
@@ -951,7 +951,8 @@ struct fman_hm_vlan_route_ent {
 	u16			vid;
 	u16			tpid;
 	u8			pcp;
-	bool			is_push;
+	bool			do_pop;
+	bool			do_push;
 	u8			src_mac[ETH_ALEN];
 	u8			dst_mac[ETH_ALEN];
 	u8			port_id;
@@ -963,19 +964,21 @@ static LIST_HEAD(fman_hm_vlan_route_cache);
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(fman_hm_vlan_route_lock);

 static struct fman_hm_vlan_route_ent *
-fman_hm_vlan_route_lookup(struct fman *fm, bool is_push, u16 vid, u16 tpid,
-			  u8 pcp, const u8 *src_mac, const u8 *dst_mac,
+fman_hm_vlan_route_lookup(struct fman *fm, bool do_pop, bool do_push,
+			  u16 vid, u16 tpid, u8 pcp,
+			  const u8 *src_mac, const u8 *dst_mac,
 			  u32 egress_tx_fqid)
 {
 	struct fman_hm_vlan_route_ent *v;

 	list_for_each_entry(v, &fman_hm_vlan_route_cache, node) {
 		if (v->fm == fm &&
-		    v->is_push == is_push &&
+		    v->do_pop == do_pop &&
+		    v->do_push == do_push &&
 		    v->egress_tx_fqid == egress_tx_fqid &&
 		    ether_addr_equal(v->src_mac, src_mac) &&
 		    ether_addr_equal(v->dst_mac, dst_mac) &&
-		    (!is_push ||
+		    (!do_push ||
 		     (v->vid == vid && v->tpid == tpid && v->pcp == pcp)))
 			return v;
 	}
@@ -1004,12 +1007,17 @@ static void fman_hm_vlan_route_l3(struct fman_hm_spec *spec, unsigned int i,
 /*
  * fman_hm_vlan_route_get - resolve (and refcount) the shared combined
  * VLAN-edit + L3-forward HM node for a routed-VLAN adjacency, installing it on
- * first use.  @is_push selects PUSH (@vid/@tpid/@pcp inserted after the L2
- * rebuild) vs POP (strip the ingress tag before the rebuild).  @dst_mac/@src_mac
- * are the egress next-hop and egress-port MACs.  On success *handle receives the
- * HMTD MURAM offset for a CC leaf hm_handle.  Sleepable; process context only.
+ * first use.  @do_pop and @do_push are independent: POP-only strips the
+ * ingress tag before the L2/L3 rebuild; PUSH-only inserts (@vid/@tpid/@pcp)
+ * after it; BOTH set builds a same-port VID-to-VID TRANSLATE chain (strip the
+ * old tag, rebuild L2/L3, insert the new tag last) -- e.g. two 802.1Q vifs on
+ * one physical port routing between each other. At least one of @do_pop/
+ * @do_push must be set. @dst_mac/@src_mac are the egress next-hop and
+ * egress-port MACs. On success *handle receives the HMTD MURAM offset for a
+ * CC leaf hm_handle. Sleepable; process context only.
  */
-int fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, bool is_push,
+int fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id,
+			   bool do_pop, bool do_push,
 			   u16 vid, u16 tpid, u8 pcp,
 			   const u8 *src_mac, const u8 *dst_mac,
 			   u32 egress_tx_fqid, u32 *handle)
@@ -1017,6 +1025,7 @@ int fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, bool is_push,
 	struct fman_hm_vlan_route_ent *v;
 	struct fman_hm_spec spec;
 	struct fman_hm_op *op;
+	unsigned int n;
 	int err;

 	if (!fm || !src_mac || !dst_mac || !handle)
@@ -1024,12 +1033,14 @@ int fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, bool is_push,
 	*handle = 0;
 	if (!fman_hm_caps_supported())
 		return -ENOTSUPP;
-	if (is_push && (vid == 0 || vid > 4094))
+	if (!do_pop && !do_push)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (do_push && (vid == 0 || vid > 4094))
 		return -EINVAL;

 	mutex_lock(&fman_hm_vlan_route_lock);

-	v = fman_hm_vlan_route_lookup(fm, is_push, vid, tpid, pcp,
+	v = fman_hm_vlan_route_lookup(fm, do_pop, do_push, vid, tpid, pcp,
 				      src_mac, dst_mac, egress_tx_fqid);
 	if (v) {
 		refcount_inc(&v->refcount);
@@ -1044,22 +1055,30 @@ int fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, bool is_push,
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}

+	/*
+	 * Op order matches the vendor fill_actions convention (strip before,
+	 * insert after the L2/L3 rebuild): STRIP (if popping) -> RMV_ETHERNET
+	 * + INSRT_GENERIC(L2) + IPV4_FORWARD -> INSERT (if pushing). A
+	 * translate chain is simply both ends present; the L3 rebuild in the
+	 * middle is identical to the single-edit cases. Max 5 of
+	 * FMAN_HM_MAX_OPS(8).
+	 */
 	memset(&spec, 0, sizeof(spec));
-	if (is_push) {
-		/* rebuild L2 first, then push the tag onto the new header */
-		fman_hm_vlan_route_l3(&spec, 0, dst_mac, src_mac);
-		op = &spec.ops[3];
+	n = 0;
+	if (do_pop)
+		spec.ops[n++].type = FMAN_HM_OP_VLAN_STRIP;
+
+	fman_hm_vlan_route_l3(&spec, n, dst_mac, src_mac);
+	n += 3;
+
+	if (do_push) {
+		op = &spec.ops[n++];
 		op->type = FMAN_HM_OP_VLAN_INSERT;
 		op->vlan_insert.vlan_id = vid;
 		op->vlan_insert.tpid = tpid ? tpid : 0x8100;
 		op->vlan_insert.pcp = pcp & 0x7;
-		spec.num_ops = 4;
-	} else {
-		/* strip the ingress tag first, then rebuild L2 for the route */
-		spec.ops[0].type = FMAN_HM_OP_VLAN_STRIP;
-		fman_hm_vlan_route_l3(&spec, 1, dst_mac, src_mac);
-		spec.num_ops = 4;
 	}
+	spec.num_ops = n;

 	err = fman_hm_node_install(fm, port_id, &spec, &v->handle);
 	if (err) {
@@ -1073,7 +1092,8 @@ int fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, bool is_push,
 	v->vid = vid;
 	v->tpid = tpid ? tpid : 0x8100;
 	v->pcp = pcp & 0x7;
-	v->is_push = is_push;
+	v->do_pop = do_pop;
+	v->do_push = do_push;
 	v->port_id = port_id;
 	ether_addr_copy(v->src_mac, src_mac);
 	ether_addr_copy(v->dst_mac, dst_mac);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h
index 7cb43afce..9144232fc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h
@@ -403,20 +403,25 @@ int  fman_hm_vlan_put(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, u32 handle);

 /**
  * fman_hm_vlan_route_get - combined VLAN-edit + L3 next-hop HM node for a
- *                          ROUTED-VLAN adjacency (T-M6-8 R4a)
- * @is_push:        true = PUSH tag (after L2 rebuild); false = POP (before)
- * @vid/@tpid/@pcp: pushed tag params (PUSH only)
- * @src_mac:        egress-port source MAC for the rebuilt L2 header
- * @dst_mac:        next-hop destination MAC for the rebuilt L2 header
- * @egress_tx_fqid: egress TX FQ (dedup key)
- * @handle:         on success, HMTD MURAM offset for a CC leaf hm_handle
- *
- * Builds one HMTD that does the tag edit AND {RMV_ETHERNET, INSRT_GENERIC(L2),
- * IPV4_FORWARD(dec_ttl,l4_csum)} - everything a routed-VLAN frame needs.  Use
- * fman_hm_vlan_get() (VLAN-only) for a bridged VLAN flow instead.  Refcounted;
+ *                          ROUTED-VLAN adjacency (T-M6-8 R4a; translate R4d)
+ * @do_pop:          strip the ingress tag before the L2/L3 rebuild
+ * @do_push:         insert (@vid/@tpid/@pcp) after the L2/L3 rebuild
+ * @vid/@tpid/@pcp:  pushed tag params (@do_push only)
+ * @src_mac:         egress-port source MAC for the rebuilt L2 header
+ * @dst_mac:         next-hop destination MAC for the rebuilt L2 header
+ * @egress_tx_fqid:  egress TX FQ (dedup key)
+ * @handle:          on success, HMTD MURAM offset for a CC leaf hm_handle
+ *
+ * @do_pop and @do_push are independent -- POP-only, PUSH-only, or BOTH (a
+ * same-port VID-to-VID TRANSLATE, e.g. two 802.1Q vifs on one physical port
+ * routing to each other) are all valid; at least one must be set. Builds one
+ * HMTD that does the tag edit(s) AND {RMV_ETHERNET, INSRT_GENERIC(L2),
+ * IPV4_FORWARD(dec_ttl,l4_csum)} - everything a routed-VLAN frame needs. Use
+ * fman_hm_vlan_get() (VLAN-only) for a bridged VLAN flow instead. Refcounted;
  * sleepable; process context.
  */
-int  fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id, bool is_push,
+int  fman_hm_vlan_route_get(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id,
+			    bool do_pop, bool do_push,
 			    u16 vid, u16 tpid, u8 pcp,
 			    const u8 *src_mac, const u8 *dst_mac,
 			    u32 egress_tx_fqid, u32 *handle);
